please refer to the SLIM paper, we are using the same source code with no adjustments on default parameters or the code, you will see examples of distributions where simulation and tests were based on. Since it doesn't always work without adjusting the parameters in the extreme cases we put an alternative, slim=FALSE (maybe it should even be the default).  I think in your case it could be a problem of non-uniform coverage over p-values, i.e. gaps in the histogram. Just use slim=FALSE when in doubt.

Best,
Altuna

