In-Reply-To: <PWpoffM4Mww.OyL9ltNZcDwJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
References: <PWpoffM4Mww.OyL9ltNZcDwJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/methylkit_discussion/c/PWpoffM4Mww/m/69qp7UFV6zEJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

Filtering the bases before performing 'unite' may not give desired results in this case.

In cases of low coverage, the following sequence of steps may be of some help:
Read every CpG (no coverage cutoff)
Remove CpG with extremely high coverage using 'normalizeCoverage'
Perform 'unite' (destrand=T)
Filter CpGs with a given threshold across all the samples

Hope this helps!

Regards,
Kalyan

